 "final_result": "Built a complete three-script Python workflow for cubic perovskite SrTiO3 (Pm-3m, #221) from scratch.\n\nMaterials Project ID: mp-5229\nAtom count: 5 before and after primitive-cell reduction (already primitive; space group Pm-3m unchanged)\n\nWorkflow outline:\n1. generate_structures.py: Read the base CIF with ase.io.read, generated 51 structures (structure_000.cif through structure_050.cif). Structure 000 is unperturbed; structures 001-050 have random atomic displacements (thermal motion at 300 K, with species-specific amplitudes: O moves most, Sr least) plus small random lattice strain. Each structure has nat=5, ntyp=3 (asserted per structure).\n2. setup_jobs.py: For each structure NNN, created calculations/NNN/ with pseudopotential files, kpath.json (from chem_llm.kpath), pw.in (SCF), bands.in (NSCF bands), and bands_post.in (bands.x). All QE inputs written with ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in. Key settings: ecutwfc=92 Ry (2\u00d746 Ha max cutoff), ecutrho=368 Ry, nbnd=40 (\u226520 occupied bands), occupations='fixed' (semiconductor), conv_thr=1e-8 Ry, SCF k-mesh 7\u00d77\u00d77 (computed via scf_kmesh), bands k-path from kp_kpts(kp).\n3. plot_bands.py: Read band data with chem_llm.kpath.plot_axis, read SCF output with chem_llm.qe_output.read_pw_out, computed VBM/CBM/gap with band_edges, and plotted the band structure with matplotlib. Saved to calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nASE functions used:\n- ase.io.read / ase.io.write for CIF I/O\n- ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in for pw.x input files\n- ase.Atoms for structure representation\n\nBand gap obtained: 1.84 eV (VBM=9.832 eV, CBM=11.672 eV, aligned to VBM)\n\nScientific assumptions:\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials (all elements Z<54, no spin-orbit physics targeted)\n- PBEsol functional, stringent accuracy, norm-conserving pseudopotentials\n- occupations='fixed' (SrTiO3 is a semiconductor with ~1.77 eV gap, not a metal)\n- 300 K thermal displacements (room temperature, where the cubic perovskite phase is stable)\n- ecutwfc=92 Ry (2\u00d746 Ha, max of all elements per INVARIANT 5)\n\nItems needing expert review:\n- The band gap of 1.84 eV is slightly higher than the experimental ~1.77 eV, which is typical for DFT with PBEsol\n- The thermal displacement amplitudes are approximate (based on typical Debye-Waller factors for SrTiO3)\n- The k-mesh density (7\u00d77\u00d77) is reasonable for a 5-atom cell but could be refined for higher accuracy",
